# Pinned mybigday/llama.rn revision that produced the vendored rn-* glue in
# llama-kt/src/main/cpp/ and whose llama.cpp patches bootstrap.sh applies.
#
# v0.13.0-rc.9: https://github.com/mybigday/llama.rn/releases/tag/v0.13.0-rc.9
# (the commit the tag points to)
#
# Coupled with third_party/llama.cpp: this revision vendors llama.cpp v0.8.0 (b11960),
# 8642541b255bfb5dc39cd351a178be09013a55d6, the same commit as our submodule; its
# vendor/VERSIONS says so and bootstrap.sh refuses to run when the two disagree.
# The rn-* files are copied verbatim, then get the same LM_ rewrite as the rest;
# scripts/patches/llama.cpp/*.patch go on an export of the submodule before the copy.
# rn-tts.cpp is left out (it needs codec.cpp, see bootstrap.sh).
#
# To bump: pick the new llama.rn revision, put its full sha here, move the
# llama.cpp submodule to the LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT in its vendor/VERSIONS, re-run
# bootstrap.sh, and re-port patches/ where the vendored sources moved.
